Original commit body from 9a391bb11f0f6fbf6e1fd85e56b200dad7bf9389:

INV-kurup's name-slot limb. id-format:F3's "Symbol.id name-slot is
empty" advisory came from four producers on grpc, and the same pass
found grpc's one id_format error:

  - starlark.py: a deps label was pasted raw into the dst
    (`starlark:BUILD::utils`), which is no id. Nothing resolved it, and
    boundary synthesis gave 479 depends_on edges one nameless
    `starlark:<unknown>:0-0::external_symbol`. Labels are now collected in
    pass 1 and resolved once every package's targets are known: `:name`,
    `name`, `//pkg:name` and `//pkg` (= //pkg:pkg) go to the declared
    target. Any other label (`@repo//...`, `@repo`, a target a macro
    makes) is an unresolved edge to
    starlark:<@repo//pkg | //pkg>:0-0:<name>. The label stays in
    meta["build_label"], and `//pkg:` makes no edge.
  - cpp.py: `enum : uint16_t { ... }`. tree-sitter fills the absent name
    with a zero-width MISSING type_identifier, which read as '' and gave
    `::enum` plus owner-less `::kA` fields. A MISSING name is now no name.
  - ruby.py: error recovery's MISSING method (`foo.`) gave a calls edge to
    `ruby:external:0-0::`. A call with no callee name now emits no edge.
  - py.py: a call-expression base (`class X(collections.namedtuple(...))`)
    formats as "" and gave `extends` to `python:external:0-0::`. It names no
    class, so it gets no edge.
  - cpp.py: a base class split across lines kept its newline and
    indentation, which ended up in an external id
    (`cpp:...EventEngine::\n    Endpoint:0-0:TelemetryInfo`). Whitespace
    around `::` is dropped.

Live on this branch: `hypergumbo run` on grpc gives id_format violations
10 -> 0. starlark depends_on resolves 14,328 of 15,572 (before: 0, raw labels).

Found alongside and filed, not fixed: INV-zopiz (ruby, kotlin and go
drop a file with no symbols before the edge pass).

